/-
Fmt/Rules8Known.lean: a chain in a file, with a tree and an opening in it. The reader of
Fmt/Rules8.lean is tested on files that another program has made.

Definitions and guards only; made by a program from that other program's files: no value here was
typed by hand. No Mathlib.
(In this head "the programs" are the C++ implementation that comes with this Lean code, and "the
format page" is docs/format/FORMAT.md, which comes with the programs.)

The reader (`wholeChain`, Fmt/Rules8.lean) is the verifier's parser of a proof file: round by
round it recomputes the hash chain from which the challenges are drawn, tests the proof of work
and checks every Merkle opening against its root. The toy of this file is a small chain made up for
tests. A test (#guard) is an evaluation made while the file compiles; the compile fails if the
result moves; it leaves no theorem. A guard is such a test.

The page: an edition of the format page that is not the one that ships; not held against that page.
The files here are this library's own toy's, not the programs': they were made, byte for byte, by a
program that calls the page's own twin in Python, independently of these Lean files.
The same program made every value in between: the digest of the parameters, the run's value, the
values of the chain, the positions and the given digests.
(The page's own known answer for a chain in a file is in Fmt/Rules8.lean.)

Main names:
  `Toy8K.spec`: the toy. It has field 2, label 7, random bytes in the file, the page's toys'
    configuration (`Toy4.cfg`) and two rounds.
    Round 1: the message is one root. Its tree has depth 4, number 0, three base-field elements a
      column and salts of 40 bytes. The round has 8 bits of work, and three positions below 16 are
      drawn. In the file the opening at the list of these positions comes after the nonce.
    Round 2: the message is one element of the extension field, s. The verifier's message is empty.
  `Toy8K.honest`, `Toy8K.honest2`, `Toy8K.read`.

What the guards check: the honest file: read, with the values that the other program printed; a
second honest file, of another length: the length of a file depends on the draw; 19 altered
copies: 17 are refused by the reader; 2 are read: they differ from an honest file in the value of
the last message alone, which no rule of the format tests (its spelling is tested: alt-13 is
refused): only the protocol's decision can refuse them, and that is no part of this reader.

Limits: this file says nothing on the programs' own files: its sources include none.
This file does not say which check of the reader refuses a copy (Fmt/Toy1.lean has that).
The programs' own files of the first toy are held as bytes, or listed, in Fmt/M1ProgPTFiles.lean,
Fmt/M1ProgPRFiles.lean and Fmt/M1ProgPFFiles.lean.
The honest proof of each set is read by the strict reader, with the values taken from the programs'
lists of the plan, the digests and the chain read from the file or recomputed, in
Fmt/M1EnginePT.lean, Fmt/M1EnginePR.lean and Fmt/M1EnginePF.lean; and all are judged in
Fmt/M1FullProg.lean, Run/PlanQSFProg.lean and files Run/M1Engine*.lean.
-/
import Fmt.Rules8

namespace Fmt
namespace Toy8K

def plan : Plan where
  field := .two
  salt := 40
  nonce := 8
  posB := 0
  samples := 0
  saved := 1
  entries := [
    { name := "toy: positions", work := 8, msg := 32, roots := 1, poss := 3, logN := 4 },
    { name := "toy: nothing", msg := 24 } ]

def spec : Spec where
  label := 7
  plan := plan
  params := paramsBytes plan Toy4.cfg []
  statement := items [("toy: claim", ext (1, 2, 3))]
  rand := .inFile
  cfg := Toy4.cfg
  rounds := [
    { entry := plan.entries.getD 0 default, kind := .positions, items := [.root],
      opens := [({ a := 4, W := 3, tree := 0 }, .own 0)] },
    { entry := plan.entries.getD 1 default, kind := .nothing, items := [.e] } ]

def read (s : String) : Option ChainOut := wholeChain (m := Id) formatHash spec (unhex s)

def honest : String := ""
def honest2 : String := ""

end Toy8K

open Toy8K in
#guard spec.ok
open Toy8K in
#guard (unhex honest).size = 512 && (unhex honest2).size = 480

-- the honest file: the digest of the parameters, the run's value, the first value, the value behind round 2
open Toy8K in
#guard ((read honest).map fun o => (hex o.pd, o.run.map hex, hex o.rho0, hex o.rho)) =
  some ("ea7dd651ee7905f1a6a0ba17ec9e384f651766d33c0cedaa082d6019a60af476", some "f7baeb7d1660e0ad5119c68da6d514a557cd59c60cc151cddcf6028486ff801f",
    "859319d1a3c364e3bd1ee29afbe8d1b2e704b8136655150c579449cb3fb776d3", "58f979c24596f408217cea4c8b5674849bb7cf2a3c724d300cd1db95d6fac945")
-- round 1: the nonce, the positions as drawn, the list
open Toy8K in
#guard ((read honest).bind fun o => o.rounds[0]?.map fun r => (r.nonce, r.drawn.poss, r.list)) = some (57, [3, 15, 8], [3, 8, 15])
-- its opening: the list, the columns, the numbers of salts and of given digests, the root
open Toy8K in
#guard ((read honest).bind fun o => o.rounds[0]?.bind fun r => r.opens.head?.map fun x => (x.2.1, x.2.2.cols, x.2.2.salts.length, x.2.2.given.length, hex x.2.2.root)) =
  some ([3, 8, 15], [[4, 6, 7], [9, 16, 7], [16, 30, 7]], 3, 7, "4c9ba0664f4d73c58082e23e7445acd360498577414dcc7d4a4c5b5dccc367b8")
-- all given digests, in the walk's order
open Toy8K in
#guard ((read honest).bind fun o => o.rounds[0]?.bind fun r => r.opens.head?.map fun x => x.2.2.given.map hex) =
  some ["f7d44dd626eb0c145d13e843a55d9516e1214f62273b77e95b747a4bbb76049d", "6d3ed99a9bd4557d71d23ebc9bc1a604d744fe1f83fcecf04f04ffafe32dcc32", "f73e5ce4584f1a73b6d37e4587e580372886cf35ad4f0fe6b6565e9c998939e1", "fd31e1a6d8ea52829253cc678ccb74072a14cc98ed24441817e052467eb52119", "db718904075b6e164aa87dd3d19aa9879442de5abc70e1b32b638a170f09f9cf", "36aa5c581e551d9a4048ca1bc03b8f0fe746e72a1e2838435751b76a64224696", "e0163aeb56fc5004a33f745487d1aefe9b8214c64e3293130050a9fd268475de"]
-- round 2: the message
open Toy8K in
#guard ((read honest).bind fun o => o.rounds[1]?.map fun r => r.vals) = some [.e (30, 54, 24)]
-- the second honest file is read too
open Toy8K in
#guard (read honest2).isSome
-- the honest file under another claim is refused
open Toy8K in
#guard (wholeChain (m := Id) formatHash { spec with statement := items [("toy: claim", ext (1, 2, 4))] } (unhex honest)).isNone

/-! ## The altered copies -/

-- alt-01: byte 0 of the random bytes, bit 0 flipped
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-02: byte 0 of the root, bit 0 flipped
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-03: the nonce 58 for 57: it fails the work test
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-04: the nonce 310 for 57: the next one that passes the work test
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-05: byte 0 of the column at 3, bit 0 flipped
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-06: byte 0 of the salt at 3, bit 0 flipped
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-07: byte 0 of the given digest (4, 2), bit 0 flipped. The pair is (depth, place)
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-08: byte 0 of s, bit 0 flipped. The copy is read (only a decision of the protocol can refuse
-- it)
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isSome

-- alt-09: the file one byte short
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-10: the file one byte long (a zero byte behind it)
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-11: the given digest (4, 2) and the given digest (4, 9) swapped
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-12: EXTRA: the first word of the column at 3 is p (no spelling of an element)
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-13: EXTRA: the first word of s is s_0 + p (the same element, another word)
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-14: EXTRA: byte 0 of the random bytes flipped and the nonce searched anew (52): the work test
-- passes
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-15: EXTRA: byte 0 of the root flipped and the nonce searched anew (175): the work test passes
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-16: EXTRA: another row f (column 0 is (5, 5, 5)), all made by the rules, but s is one too
-- large in e_2 (its third word): only the decision can refuse. The copy is read (only a decision of
-- the protocol can refuse it)
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isSome

-- alt-17: RE-CUT: opening and s are made anew for the positions that the altered chain draws.
-- The nonce is 58, which fails the work test. It draws the positions [14, 5, 11]. Opening and s are
-- made for them from the honest tree: only the work test can refuse (the guard holds that the copy
-- is refused, not by which check)
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-18: RE-CUT: byte 0 of the root is flipped, and the least nonce is searched anew (175).
-- Opening and s are made for the new positions [4, 11, 6] from the honest tree: the walk ends in
-- the honest root, not in the sent one
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

-- alt-19: RE-CUT: byte 0 of the random bytes flipped, the least nonce anew (52), opening and s for
-- the new positions [1, 1, 2], from the honest tree, whose leaves hold the old run's value: the
-- walk does not end in the root
open Toy8K in
#guard (read "").isNone

end Fmt
